In instrumentation/redisson/redisson-common-3.0/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/redisson/common/v3_0/RedissonErrorCapture.java, extract the current CRLF scanning loop into a private static findCrlf(ByteBuf input, int start) helper. Use a forward for loop, a positive match for the adjacent CR and LF bytes, an immediate return of the CR index when found, and return -1 when no complete terminator is present. Keep that helper immediately after its caller in the utility class.

Within parseServerErrorType's existing try block, use the names replyStart, lineStart and lineEnd. Check the '-' marker at replyStart, set lineStart to replyStart + 1, call findCrlf(input, lineStart), return null when lineEnd == -1, and pass only input.toString(lineStart, lineEnd - lineStart, UTF_8) to RedisErrorPrefix.extract. The agreed code shape is:

```java
int replyStart = input.readerIndex();
if (input.getByte(replyStart) != '-') {
  return null;
}

int lineStart = replyStart + 1;
int lineEnd = findCrlf(input, lineStart);
if (lineEnd == -1) {
  return null;
}

return RedisErrorPrefix.extract(
    input.toString(lineStart, lineEnd - lineStart, UTF_8));
```

